From 9d17c56dfce8531fdc0536ca10ace09b1c760396 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Unive Tien <unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Nov 2025 08:48:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] yosemite4: pldm: remove firmware update entry

Description:
Remove the firmware update entry from the inventory manager before the
feature implementation is complete.

Motivation:
Related to JIRA ticket YV4T1M-2210, BMC mfg-tool displays excessive and
unclear system firmware information, which is the new firmware update
entry preserved for enhanced firmware update features but not yet fully
implemented. To avoid confusion, we decided to remove this entry for now
and reintroduce it later when the feature is ready.

Tested:
Tested on the Yosemite4 platform to ensure that the firmware update entry
is no longer exposed on D-Bus, and verified that other inventory
functionalities remain unaffected.
---
 fw-update/inventory_manager.cpp | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fw-update/inventory_manager.cpp b/fw-update/inventory_manager.cpp
index 7975f7a..47ae909 100644
--- a/fw-update/inventory_manager.cpp
+++ b/fw-update/inventory_manager.cpp
@@ -676,11 +676,6 @@ void InventoryManager::getFirmwareParameters(
         {
             auto componentName = firmwareDeviceNameMap.at(eid) + "_Component_" +
                                  std::to_string(compIdentifier);
-
-            firmwareInventoryManager.createFirmwareEntry(
-                SoftwareIdentifier(eid, compIdentifier), componentName,
-                utils::toString(activeCompVerStr), descriptorMap.at(eid),
-                componentInfo);
         }
         else
         {
-- 
2.47.3

